        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Reginald Engelbach, Christiane Desroches Noblecourt\n- Places: Cairo, Harageh, Egypt\n- Organizations: Egyptian Museum of Cairo\n- Roles: Egyptologist, engineer\n- Topics: archaeology, museum artifact registers\n\nFacts:\n- Reginald Engelbach excavated the cemeteries at Harageh in 1913.\n- Christiane Desroches Noblecourt was born on 17 November 1913 and was a French Egyptologist.\n- Reginald Engelbach was an English Egyptologist and engineer who lived from 9 July 1888 to 26 February 1946.\n- Reginald Engelbach is mainly known for his work at the Egyptian Museum of Cairo, especially for compiling a register of the museum's artifacts.\n- Cairo is the capital and largest city of Egypt.",
